text.section:
The following matters shall be reported within 30 days of their occurrence to the Board:

Any disciplinary action taken against a person licensed under this chapter in another state or in a federal health institution or voluntary surrender of a license in another state while under investigation;


Any malpractice judgment against a person licensed under this chapter;


Any settlement of a malpractice claim against a person licensed under this chapter; and


Any evidence that indicates a reasonable belief that a person licensed under this chapter is or may be professionally incompetent; has or may have engaged in intentional or negligent conduct that causes or is likely to cause injury to a patient or patients; has or may have engaged in unprofessional conduct; or may be mentally or physically unable to engage safely in the practice of his profession.

The following persons and entities are subject to the reporting requirements set forth in this section:

Any person licensed under this chapter who is the subject of a disciplinary action, a settlement, a judgment, or evidence for which reporting is required pursuant to this section;


Any other person licensed under this chapter, except as provided by a contract agreement with the Health Practitioners' Monitoring Program;


All health care institutions licensed by the Commonwealth;


The malpractice insurance carrier of any person who is the subject of a judgment or settlement; and


Any health maintenance organization licensed by the Commonwealth.
